# Plans must include /no-comments

Whenever you create or revise an implementation plan for this project (Plan mode, `/plan`, or any written plan before coding):

- Include an explicit final step to run `/no-comments` on the plan's scoped diff (caller files/diff, otherwise the branch/working-tree diff against `main`).
- Do not mark the plan complete, or claim implementation done, until that `/no-comments` step has been executed per `.agents/skills/no-comments/SKILL.md`.
- Keep `/no-comments` in scope for code-changing plans; skip it only for pure docs/tooling plans that touch no application source under `src/`.
